{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a74a97a464206768e4ec184ddd03c4fd0802e08ba7949fbd7a6eb4d810a6ea30", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe case of sheaves of modules is more complicated.\nThe reason is that the natural setting for defining\nthe pullback and pushforward functors, is the setting\nof ringed spaces, which we will define below. First\nwe state a few obvious lemmas.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:66607076e050b8c61c2b3b9a1d4da558611641107a4cee614a8fbcc7cdc0e843", "unit_id": "tag:008R:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_*\\mathcal{O} \\times f_*\\mathcal{F}\n\\longrightarrow\nf_*\\mathcal{F}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pushforward-presheaf-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bdfe33b2db64d8e88eb5ef6f88f17170b4bdb7d907519b1e6e1f0a02663e11cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4bbd4884469d8aa86f9d03c030de9e95b6405395e96f589ec26474b6cf688f44", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a presheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>. Let\n<MATH_0004> be a presheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nThere is a natural map of underlying presheaves of sets\n<MATH_0006>\nwhich turns <MATH_0007> into a presheaf of\n<MATH_0008>-modules. This construction is\nfunctorial in <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fc3a1a5fcf42002173b9d6cace2b0d30e72bab163b110a7f1fb9d26ce91b5e5a", "unit_id": "tag:008S:statement"}
