{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "008R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_p\\mathcal{O} \\times f_p\\mathcal{G}\n\\longrightarrow\nf_p\\mathcal{G}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f_p\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0008": "$f_p\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{G}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-presheaf-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:99a880552a3a2d441e5b0d06eb9d84b835c8b9f1e217998a28b728faa318989f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:007d24a2d344d5d5191219431dd24af4e0165d5a49881cae6e925f1925ed3ba6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a continuous map of topological spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a presheaf of rings on <MATH_0003>. Let\n<MATH_0004> be a presheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nThere is a natural map of underlying presheaves of sets\n<MATH_0006>\nwhich turns <MATH_0007> into a presheaf of <MATH_0008>-modules.\nThis construction is functorial in <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dbd4a8604303661adf8a971269280a9035cc2b15f864abc281c1618656ce8fac", "unit_id": "tag:008T:statement"}
